<section id="choose" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Go, Go+, Bravo or Tango?</h2>
  <p>Go transmits your position in ADS-L, the European standard for sharing position by radio. It shows ADS-L and FLARM traffic. FLARM is a position-sharing system widely used in gliding. Bravo detects Mode S and ADS-B transponders. Aircraft with ADS-B transmit their position by radio.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="compare">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">If you want to</th><th scope="col">Choose</th><th scope="col">Hardware to order</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">See ADS-L and FLARM traffic on a pocket radar and transmit your position in ADS-L.</th><td><%= link_to_page "features", label: "Go" %></td><td>LilyGO T-Echo</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Keep the same radar and add sound and vibration to the on-screen alert.</th><td><%= link_to_page "features", label: "Go+" %></td><td>LilyGO T-Echo Plus</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">See ADS-B traffic in a compatible navigation app.</th><td><%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "Bravo" %></td><td>MeshTracker X1</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Add ADS-B traffic to the radar on Go or Go+.</th><td><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "Tango" %></td><td>A T-Echo or T-Echo Plus and a MeshTracker X1, bought separately</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p><strong>For Go and Go+, check that the listing says 868 MHz and BME280 barometer.</strong> Some variants aren&rsquo;t suitable for skyBlip. The BME280 is required for skyBlip compliance.</p>
